Google <a href="https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/photos/google-photos-updates/">today said</a> its digital wardrobe option is available in the Google <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/photos/">Photos</a> iOS app in the U.S., India, and Brazil.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1046284" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/04/google-photos-wardrobe.jpg" alt="" width="2096" height="1178" /><br/>
Google first <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/29/google-photos-ai-wardrobe/">announced the feature</a> back in April, but it was limited to Android users until now. The wardrobe option uses AI to pull images of clothing from the Google &zwnj;Photos&zwnj; library, organizing them into a digital closet.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1046285" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/04/google-photos-wardrobe-app.jpg" alt="" width="1959" height="1102" /><br/>
Users can put items together to create outfits and virtually try them on.<br/>
<br/>
The app shows clothing items in a new Wardrobe section in the Collections tab. Clothing can also be viewed in specific categories like tops or bottoms. Items of clothing can be mixed and matched, and the results can be shared with friends or saved to a moodboard.<br/>
<br/>
